(49, 52, 101)
```
The minimum possible value of \(a_1 + a_2\) such that the sequence \(a_{n + 2} = \frac{a_n + 2009}{1 + a_{n + 1}}\) produces positive integers for all \(n \ge 1\) is \(\boxed{101}\). This occurs when \(a_1 = 49\) and \(a_2 = 52\).

